It provides meta-prompting. It creates a UI using the Fluentpro Library. Fluentpro Document:



In the UI, create a section called "Villains" In this section, place (or create if it doesn't already exist) a dropdown menu. This dropdown menu will contain all the items within this folder: workspace.MobSpawnGroup, and if a specific item(everyone who has an item (ChestRef) inside the "Spawn" area. ) is found within one of those folders, it will appear in the dropdown menu.   Create another section called: "Mobs near player" in this section there will be another drop-down menu and it will scan everything within this model:workspace.Mob And it will appear in the dropdown menu; if there are models with the same name, it won't show more than two. Only one. Create a section called "Weapons"; in that section, there will be another dropdown that will scan that folder:workspace.NpcWeapon And it will appear in the dropdown menu. Create another section called: "island" And there will be a dropdown that will scan this folder:workspace.island(folder).


In all drop-downs (except for the island and weapon section drop-downs), the drop-down will be multi-item, meaning you can choose more than one.
Below all dropdown there will be a refresh button. and a toggle button (on when activated, off when deactivated) For the mob near player and villains sections. When the button is activated in the following sections: Villains, Mobs near player, it will execute a code to teleport and remain on top of the models or the chest(in the case of the Villains section) Which the player chose. And in those sections there will be a textbox or slider or something else to increase and decrease the distance between the player and the mob. Important: the player will be lying on top of the mob, facing it.

In the Island and Weapon sections, there will only be one clickable button, and when clicked, it will teleport you to the island or weapon NPC you selected.
